From e370f8ee4b8911453a1893ad772fa6583f7e1c60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:48:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] move guard: unchecked cause on spent budget/timeout,
 shared repin leaving rule, park-pin owner test (PR #1792 review nits)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-ups from PR #1792's review (pullrequestreview-5885034090), card t_01a1d2add77deeff.

1. kanban_move_pool._BudgetSpent subclassed ValueError, so a git budget spent inside
   pushed_on_remote was swallowed (it fails toward False) and tree_state reported
   "unpushed commits in <p>" instead of "unchecked worktree <p>". It is now a plain
   Exception. tree_state also reads "unchecked" when a dirty/unpushed check returned
   True only because its git timed out (the worktree_ops checks fail toward True on a
   timeout, which is no evidence of state), and when pushed_on_remote's git calls failed
   toward False as the budget ran out. Every case still counts as state (fail safe);
   only the cause text changes.
2. The worker-first queue repin in move_queued treated any labels other than exactly
   [machine:<origin>] as leaving; check() uses "this machine is not among the matches".
   Both now call kanban_move.leaves_here(me, matches); the repin computes matches from
   the registry with the origin included (it is queued). An exact [machine:<origin>]
   still stays (the origin need not be registered) and an unreadable registry counts as
   leaving (the guard runs).
3. card_trees()'s other-card owner filter also governs park pins (kanban_park_pin passes
   the park text). That is intended: a reviewer parking while naming the implementer's
   tree must not pin the reviewer; the implementer's own park pins it. Now covered by a
   park-path test, both owners.

RED (sources at origin/main, new test file): 5 failed — the three cause-text tests read
"unpushed commits in"/"dirty worktree", the repin-includes-me test is refused
unpushed_state_here, _repin_leaves is missing. Item 3's tests pass on main (confirmation).
GREEN: 9/9. Consumers: 25 test files importing kanban_move/_pool/park_pin, 659 passed.
---
